:"DTX3 functions as an E3 ubiquitin ligase (Takeyama et al., 2003 [PubMed 12670957]).[supplied by OMIM, Nov 2009].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q8N9I9","text":"Functions as an ubiquitin ligase protein, and regulates Notch signaling (PubMed:35782979, PubMed:40127622). By promoting the ubiquitination and subsequent degradation of target proteins, it can block activation of the Notch signaling pathway, potentially acting as a tumor suppressor in human cancers (PubMed:31854042, PubMed:35782979, PubMed:40127622). [Isoform 3]: Involved in the angiogenic EPHB4 kinase degradation in cancer cell."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}